The function is already a minimal getter; I kept the same lookup but wrote it as a single ternary so the compiler emits one branchless pointer test and no extra basic block, which is marginally cheaper when `GetField` is not inlined.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsFavoriteValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(8);
        return (FIT_NULL != field) ? field->IsValueValid() : FIT_FALSE;
    }
```